WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.640
The checkout

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:01.920
button behaves differently

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:02.560
today.

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:02.960
You have

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:03.360
found a

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.400
likely commit in

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.120
the history.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:05.760
Now open

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:06.160
that one

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:06.720
record with

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.760
Git Show to

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:08.480
inspect what

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.880
it actually contains.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:11.400
Think of

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:11.960
history as

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:12.360
a shelf

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.080
of records.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:13.880
Show opens

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.440
a selected

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:14.840
record for

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:15.880
a closer look.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:16.200
For a

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:16.680
commit,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.000
you can

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.120
inspect its message,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:18.680
author,

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:19.080
date,

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.480
and recorded changes.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:22.560
Imagine a

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.120
commit that

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:23.520
makes the

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.160
button wait

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.600
for payment confirmation.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.640
Its message gives

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.360
context.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.400
Its patch shows

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.440
the recorded file

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.240
changes.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:30.960
This before

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.080
and after diagram

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.520
illustrates the idea.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.720
Inspecting the commit

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.120
does not

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:35.600
edit your

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.520
current files.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:38.480
Read the

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.600
message alongside the

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.240
change.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:40.800
A message

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:41.920
gives context,

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:42.240
but it

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:42.720
does not

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.000
prove every intention

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.120
or consequence.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:45.600
Find the

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.800
commit in history,

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.840
then use show

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:48.320
to inspect

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.160
the details.
